# `%` is not defined element-wise on [char]. `%` leaves the element-wise table by
# its own earlier gate (src/tychoc.c:1071 admits int and the sized ints only),
# not by the char arm at src/tychoc.c:1075 -- so this fixture pins a DIFFERENT
# line from tests/reject/char_elem_mul.ty even though the diagnostic reads the
# same. Deleting the char arm would leave this one green and that one red.
fn main():
    s := "ABC"
    a := [char_at(s, 0), char_at(s, 1)]
    b := a % a
    println(str(b[0]))
